# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# Without this the archive was 4.8 GB and the limit is 2.0 GB. Almost none of it
# was source: the repo is 32 GB, of which .claude is 23 GB and Xcode DerivedData
# from the E2E suite is another 6.4 GB. The app itself is a few megabytes.
#
# NOTE: when this file exists it REPLACES .gitignore for archive purposes, so
# everything unwanted has to be listed here even if git already ignores it —
# which is why node_modules and the native folders appear below despite being in
# .gitignore. (EAS did not honour .gitignore here: .e2e-derived and ios/ are both
# git-ignored and were uploaded anyway.)
#
# RUN EAS FROM apps/mobile, NOT THE REPO ROOT. The root has no Expo config, so
# `eas build` there prompts for a bundle identifier and scaffolds a stub app.json
# + eas.json pointing at a DIFFERENT projectId with no env vars. Two files named
# app.json, two named eas.json, and which you get depends on your cwd:
#
#     cd apps/mobile && npx eas-cli build --platform ios --profile production
#
# This file stays at the repo root because that is the directory EAS archives
# from in a monorepo, even when invoked from apps/mobile.

# Agent worktrees and session artefacts. The single biggest item at 23 GB:
# .claude/worktrees holds full copies of the repo.
.claude/

# Xcode DerivedData written by the E2E harness (scripts/e2e/run.mjs). 6.4 GB.
**/.e2e-derived/

# E2E screenshots, accessibility dumps and app logs, one directory per run.
apps/mobile/e2e/artifacts/

# Dependencies — EAS installs these itself from the lockfile.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Native output. EAS runs prebuild and pod install; Pods alone is 632 MB.
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/android/

# Build caches and local state
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
**/.expo/
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/storybook-static/

# The web app is not part of a mobile build.
apps/web/

# History, docs and design source
.git/
docs/
Requirements/
Branding/
